  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Shelter Assistance to Displaced Populations in North Kivu</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the end of 2022, the security situation in the eastern Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) has continued to deteriorate with the intensification of fighting between the March 23 Movement (M23) armed group and the Congolese armed forces, as well as the persistent activism of other armed groups and inter-communal conflicts. As a result, the DRC is facing one of the most complex and protracted humanitarian crises in the world, marked by mass displacement, critical needs in life-saving services, and severe human rights violations.Through this Central Emergency Response Fund (CERF) envelope, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is providing humanitarian assistance to populations affected by the M23 crisis in North Kivu, in the territories of Masisi and Rutshuru, specifically for a total of 7,000 households composed of 24,500 individuals. More specifically, IOM is addressing the massive shelter needs in North Kivu through the provision of emergency shelter kits to promote safer and more dignified living conditions for newly displaced people.</narrative>
  </description>
